[48.44143, "o", "\r\nHere is the prioritised audit report for the `broken-demo` charm. \r\n\r\n### 🔴 Critical (Must Fix)\r\n*   **Testing**: No unit tests exist in `tests/unit/`.\r\n\r\n### 🟠 Important (Should Fix)\r\n*   **Code Logic**: The `log-level` config option is declared in `charmcraft.yaml` but is completely ignored in the charm code.\r\n*   **Observability**: Missing all standard COS integrations (tracing, metrics, logging, dashboards) and the `ops-tracing` library.\r\n*   **Status Handling**: The charm doesn't set `BlockedStatus` for missing relations or invalid/missing configuration.\r\n*   **Operational Actions**: Missing standard lifecycle actions (`get-health`, `pause`, `resume`).\r\n*   **Testing**: No integration tests exist in `tests/integration/`.\r\n*   **Metadata**: Missing basic description, display-name, and a `README.md`.\r\n\r\n### 🟡 Enhancements (Nice to Have)\r\n*   **Code Structure**: Lacks a holistic status reconciliation method, and handlers for `config-changed` or `relation-changed` events.\r\n*   **Security**: No TLS/encryption support (via `tls-certificates`).\r\n*   **Documentation & Publishing**: Missing `icon.svg`, `LICENSE`, and links for source/issues/docs in the metadata. No formal usage or troubleshooting documentation.\r\n\r\nSince you requested no automated tasks be queued, I haven't started on any of these. Let me know which area you'd like to tackle first!\r\n"]
[50.693785, "o", "\u001b[2;37m# \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2;37m# From here cantrip would queue fix tasks, branch, and apply them\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2;37m# in disposable subagents. Gate every step with /tasks confirm.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
